@startuml
!include _style.iuml
' Adapted from reviewed presentation sources: W3-10/11/12/12a/13/13a; retry identity and independent stale fences
skinparam dpi 110
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam ArrowFontSize 17
skinparam ClassAttributeFontSize 17
skinparam ClassStereotypeFontSize 15
skinparam NoteFontSize 16
skinparam LegendFontSize 15
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam maxMessageSize 165
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 24
hide footbox
hide circle
title UC-4 · stale worker and stale result are separate fences
autonumber
participant "messaging\nprocessing" as M $PROC
participant "lifecycle\nprocessing" as L $PROC
database "Processing DB" as DB $INFRA
[-> M : finish(factory, old_work, error="Late completion")
M -> L : finish(factory, old_work, error=error,\non_change=emit_state)
L -> DB : lock_pair(session, old job, old attempt)
L -> L : db_now(session); live(pair, work.lease_token, now)
alt superseded / expired / deleted authority
 L --> M : False; no state or result change
 M -->[ : False
else current live authority
 L -> DB : terminal state + result outbox; COMMIT
 L --> M : True
 M -->[ : True
end
note over M,DB
Separate Media projection fence:
media.projections.validate_transition.
Older state_version or later version for an older
attempt_number → ignore.
Same version + identical semantic hash → no-op;
changed content → 409 rollback.
New stale message may commit inbox; projection stays
unchanged.
end note
@enduml
